{{!-- /the-faith-received/tradition/ — the traditions, and one page per
     tradition at ?t=<slug>.

     Ian, 2026-09-24, on the Confessions page's "About Baptist" link, which
     opened an author page that could not load: "Looks like we need
     tradition pages! What a great opportunity to do an overview of each
     tradition, feature their confessions and catechisms and authors."

     One template for all of them. assets/js/page/faith-tradition.js reads
     ?t=, writes the name into the h1 and the dek under it, and draws the
     overview, the documents and the authors into [data-trad-root]. The
     prose lives in assets/data/faith-received/traditions.json, where it
     can be revised without touching this file. Without ?t= the same page
     is the index of traditions. --}}

<main class="faith-received tfr-trad">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/tradition/">Traditions</a></p>
      <h1 data-trad-name>Traditions</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub" data-trad-dek>The churches whose creeds and confessions and writers the library holds. Each has an overview with its documents and its authors in the order they were written.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>

  <section class="bband tfr-trad-body">
    <div class="container" data-trad-root><p class="tfr-trad-note">Loading&hellip;</p></div>
  </section>

{{> "faith-received/_beta-band"}}
</main>
